=== file: README.md ===
# Article bullet support check

This Loom workflow summarizes supplied article text as exactly five bullets, then independently checks each bullet against the article. Unsupported claims trigger a revision and recheck, for no more than two revision rounds. If issues remain, or a model step fails, the workflow asks the human reviewer and returns `human_review`, never a verified result.

All model roles use the plan’s listed `gpt-6-luna` model. The article is treated as untrusted source data, not instructions. Agents that see article content use PII masking. There are no tools, external network calls, or automatic publishing effects.

## Run and test

Run the workflow with an article supplied as `source_material`:

```text
weave run main.loom -i source_material="Paste article text here"
```

Run the scripted workflow tests without model calls or network access:

```text
weave test main.loom
```

The run budget is capped at 16,000 tokens and 12 calls. Human review is requested for unresolved issues and handled by the Loom runtime’s normal suspend-and-resume flow.
=== end

